                      "explanation":  "When the expression looks like \\((a+b)^2\\), \\((a-b)^2\\), or \\((a+b)(a-b)\\), use the identity first. Then simplify the square-root squares and combine the rational and surd terms. This avoids a long expansion and reduces mistakes."
